#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100725 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "e092e191-84ac-5d9f-b0db-94d628a6154e" :question/math-academy-id "e-525" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny' = -\\dfrac{y}{x}, \\qquad x \\neq 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f'(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$\n\n- Substituting $y = f(x)$ and $y' = f'(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ and $y' = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048593} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050271} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050789}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} {:answer/id #uuid "241c8aac-057f-5bd8-8672-538887a90f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8022058-91f7-5a21-86f8-cda411ec1bea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95795348-591c-5f80-a9dc-9d6695fa2629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437922} {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8576006-7ef6-5181-a3ea-35a1c7c390e2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f72c83c-eb8c-5631-b3a6-b174e90aab92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437924} {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e1d7437-eee9-54ee-a6bc-2720730fc72d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b2e480d-7f17-59ba-a02c-a786007bf39b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140631" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne 5{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=4{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ (4{x}^{3}) & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =4{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df433686-7b08-5422-9159-68e30b1dd3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437926} {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927} :answer-field/id #uuid "3da2476a-cd94-5d52-b20c-ba45588a2e94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "697f7e93-3daf-5d09-aaa0-33a0a696b34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437928} {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929} :answer-field/id #uuid "13228480-d8e3-59b9-a952-c0a713529199" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bbf35f7-eca9-5cd8-a4bb-3916780464ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437930} {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4b74fc-fbff-523b-9711-9570469a2063" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47b66471-b70f-5509-8368-6a6674b74447" :question/math-academy-id "q-141078" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)={e}^{2x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ 2{e}^{2x} & =2{e}^{2x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777b71-5609-57b6-98cd-5de6ad97f13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} :answer-field/id #uuid "1754ff84-62e2-5fa6-b4ab-1a4ed225ccf5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebf7563-afa0-50f3-97cb-0e17f76f6a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} :answer-field/id #uuid "94674f44-214d-51de-8806-6b7b3a2c49aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} {:answer/id #uuid "5695c90a-25d5-5c15-8845-780cd00f9341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41c643e-8038-5852-a780-537545979885" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c28aa3d-73cf-552e-9e05-dfc5bcb67151" :question/math-academy-id "q-141080" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & \\ne 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\ne \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc440dfb-329e-5cce-98e2-d61a73c6573b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437938} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939} :answer-field/id #uuid "062dd2dc-b6ff-50a1-9e87-20f44d397210" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} {:answer/id #uuid "bfde07d3-eb9e-55be-b75d-2f6e35461ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e330e7c-b25a-5b7f-9f95-b68a2feb22aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} {:answer/id #uuid "22a53b8b-e4ab-51f5-a137-7c3a442b5a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad20673a-9803-59bc-b2e5-d66a0d3efe10" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82065c87-2fb6-51b8-8d32-9c57d0719fb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141081" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\ne {cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76321bcd-1dfe-54f5-8624-a1897a3eb02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437944} {:answer/id #uuid "74e24dca-